 ## Network use
 
-Limen uses the network for one in-app service. After the user types at least three characters in a Swiss address field, the app waits briefly and automatically sends the typed search text and ordinary network metadata to the Swiss federal swisstopo SearchServer at `https://api3.geo.admin.ch/rest/services/ech/SearchServer`. That service is operated under its own terms and privacy information. The lookup does not send protocol records, photos or signatures to Peringer. On iPhone the app makes that request through an ephemeral session, so neither the typed address nor the reply is written to a shared cache on disk.
+On Android 1.2, online address suggestions are optional and off by default. Before enabling them, the user sees a disclosure and confirms the choice. When enabled, typing at least three characters in a Swiss address field sends the search text and ordinary network metadata to the federal swisstopo SearchServer at `https://api3.geo.admin.ch/rest/services/ech/SearchServer`. Manual entry works offline. Earlier Android versions and the iPhone version start suggestions automatically after typing. Swisstopo operates under its own terms and privacy information. No records, photographs or signatures are sent to Peringer. On iPhone, an ephemeral network session avoids a shared disk cache for the query and reply.
 
